    "_why": "5 assertions in test files dated 2026-11-02 breached the set. The guard's message prefers CONVERTING an assertion to one that EXECUTES over widening the set, and that preference was applied before these were pinned: each of the 5 was read and judged individually, and the reason it is text rather than execution is recorded below. 3 of the 5 ALREADY have an executing half; the source-text half is the anchor that ties prose to evidence. The other 2 are premise tripwires, which is the case this guard's own docstring names as legitimate: 'a ratchet on a list that must not shrink is legitimately about the text'.",
    "reasons": {
      "test_a_merge_carries_its_evidence_2026-11-02.py::test_the_status_still_declares_the_evidence_it_requires": "A TRIPWIRE ON THE PRODUCT'S OWN DECLARATION. It asserts the runner still states that MERGED requires both-directions evidence and is not a duplicate claim. The subject IS that prose: if the product drops the declaration, the sibling checks rest on a rule nothing states any more, and the test's own message says to re-derive rather than keep asserting it.",
      "test_a_seat_declares_what_it_is_missing_2026-11-02.py::test_the_runner_still_carries_the_comment_this_rests_on": "A PREMISE TRIPWIRE, which is the case this guard's own docstring protects. It exists so that if the runner stops declaring the roster twice, the 2-list hazard its siblings check for no longer exists and they get re-measured instead of silently passing.",
      "test_the_preflight_refuses_an_unregistered_seat_2026-11-02.py::test_fables_values_declare_that_they_are_inherited": "ALREADY HALF-EXECUTING, and the text half has no data surface. It reads the live `MODEL_SPECS['Fable']['_provenance']` by execution; the source-text half covers 2 tables that carry their provenance only as a comment, because no field exists to hold it. Converting it would require adding that field, which is a product change and not a test repair.",
      "test_the_roster_window_bound_is_sound_2026-11-02.py::test_the_cascade_the_runner_itself_names_is_among_them": "ALREADY HALF-EXECUTING, and the text half is the anchor. It globs the archive for the run the runner's prose names, so prose and evidence cannot drift apart. The literal is what ties the 2 together; removing it leaves the glob checking a run nothing points at.",
      "test_two_seats_cannot_share_one_description_2026-11-02.py::test_the_description_does_not_contradict_the_live_dispatch": "ALREADY HALF-EXECUTING, and the text half is deliberate. It reads `MODEL_ROSTER` live and checks the DISPATCH SITE rather than a remembered string, precisely so a route change moves both together. That is the conversion this guard asks for, applied as far as the dispatch site allows."
